+When `OPENWIKI_WIKI_DIR` is inside a Git worktree, each successful source run
+commits its wiki changes with `OpenWiki-Connector`,
+`OpenWiki-Source-Instance`, and `OpenWiki-Pull-Run` provenance trailers.
+OpenWiki requires the wiki directory to be clean before it pulls connector
+state; commit, stash, or revert existing wiki changes before retrying. Ingestion
+outside a Git worktree keeps the existing no-commit behavior.
+
 - `git-repo` reads configured local repository paths and writes compact manifests.
 - `x` uses the X API directly with OAuth user-context credentials for home timeline, user posts, mentions, bookmarks, and list posts.
 - `notion` targets the hosted Notion MCP server, so users should authenticate through Notion OAuth instead of pasting a Notion token into OpenWiki.
